==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} ''[[socle#French|socle]]'', from {{etyl|it|en}} {{m|it|zoccolo||wooden shoe}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} ''[[socculus]]'', diminutive of {{m|la|soccus||sock}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈsoʊkəl/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|oʊkəl|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}
{{wikipedia}}

# {{label|en|architecture}} A low [[plinth]] or [[pedestal]] used to display a statue or other art work.
# {{label|en|mathematics}} The sum of the minimal [[submodule]]s of a given R-[[module]] of a given [[ring]] R.
# {{label|en|mathematics|group theory}} The [[subgroup]] generated by the minimal [[normal subgroup]]s of a given [[group]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|a plinth or pedestal}} [[zocco]], [[zocle]]

